Implemented behavior:
- The explicit privileged purge requires TrustedFirmId and a zero-offset UTC
  evaluation instant, with no firm-omitting overload.
- Candidate discovery and deletion remain independently scoped to the trusted
  firm. Unexpired rows and every row belonging to another firm survive.
- RetentionUntilUtc is applied as an exclusive boundary: one tick before
  survives, the boundary instant and later instants are eligible.
- Eligible record graphs are deleted under one serializable transaction and
  returned through PurgeOutcome.NoEligibleRecords() or
  PurgeOutcome.RecordsPurged(...).
- Diagnostics carry only structural record/slip counts and the opaque trusted
  firm identifier; no taxpayer display name, employer name, amount, box code,
  CRA line code, or nine-digit run is emitted.

